<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coscōnĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a Roman
				plebeian</i> gens; esp., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> C. Cosconius, <i>prætor during
				Cicero's consulate, also known as a writer on antiquities</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 6, § 39</span></i>, and
			§ 89 Müll.; <i><span class="en">Cic. Sull.
				14, 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Brut. 69,
			242</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			C. Cosconius Calidianus, <i>an inferior orator</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Brut. 69, 242</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>A writer of epigrams</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 2,
				77, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 69,
			7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
